    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">As i had no previous experience with using R in this context, i misunderstood the example as well at first. <br>It&#39;s actually an example of how to combine the brew package with rApache. You have to install the brew package <br>and add a handler for brew in your config, that runs the brew function over the file containing the code. <br>Example from the official documentation to add to your config:<br><br><b><b><b><b><b><b><pre>&lt;Directory /var/www/brew&gt;\r\n    SetHandler r-script\r\n    RHandler brew::brew\r\n&lt;/Directory&gt;<br><br></pre></b></b></b></b></b></b> If a file from the /var/www/brew folder is called by the browser, rApache will execute the brew() function from the brew package with this file as input.<br>The output includes the evaluation from everything between the &lt;%%&gt;. For more information, check ?brew if you have the package installed.<br><br>Best of luck,<br>Z</div>"
    ],
    [
